# Mobile & Responsive UI Rules

This project is used on phones (360px wide) as well as desktop. Every page and component MUST work on mobile without horizontal page scroll.

## Tables — Always Contained Scroll

Tables are wider than mobile viewports. NEVER let a table overflow the page.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — table overflows the page, causes full-page horizontal scroll
<div className="rounded-lg border">
  <Table>...</Table>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — table scrolls inside its own container
<div className="rounded-lg border overflow-x-auto">
  <Table className="min-w-[640px]">...</Table>
</div>
```

- Wrap every `<Table>` in a container with `overflow-x-auto`
- Set `min-w-[Npx]` on `<Table>` so columns don't collapse (typically 500–700px)
- NEVER set fixed widths on table containers that exceed viewport

## Layout Containers — Prevent Overflow

- The `<main>` wrapper in the dashboard layout MUST include `min-w-0 max-w-full overflow-x-hidden`
- Content wrappers (`<div>` inside `<main>`) MUST include `min-w-0 max-w-full`
- Use `p-4 sm:p-6` for content padding (tighter on mobile)

## Sheet / Sidebar (Mobile Drawer)

- The mobile sidebar uses `<Sheet>` from base-ui. The backdrop MUST be opaque enough to hide content behind it (`bg-black/50` minimum)
- Sidebar width on mobile: use viewport-relative units (`85vw`) not fixed `rem` values
- Always pass `dir="rtl"` to `<Sidebar>` since the Sheet portals outside the RTL root
- Avoid `backdrop-blur` on mobile overlays — causes GPU rendering artifacts (black strips) on some Android devices
- Use `h-dvh` instead of `h-full` for Sheet panels to account for mobile browser address bar

## General Mobile Rules

- Never use fixed pixel widths on flex children without `min-w-0`
- Prefer `truncate` on text that might overflow (e.g., page titles in headers)
- Use `flex-wrap` on toolbar rows with multiple controls
- Test every new page/component at 360×820 viewport (Tecno KI7 / typical Android)
